-- 1. self-join: column requirements are unioned across both plan leaves
-- miss (allowed):
1
2
-- hit (both columns still granted, allowed):
1
2
-- hit after revoking SELECT(b) must be denied:
ACCESS_DENIED
-- 2. scalar subquery: only table-level SELECT lets the plan be cached
-- first run (allowed):
1	300
2	300
-- second run with only column grants is allowed as well (not cached):
1	300
2	300
-- revoking the column read by the scalar subquery denies the query:
ACCESS_DENIED
-- after granting table-level SELECT the query is allowed:
1	300
2	300
-- 3. revoked access evicts the denied entry and releases its quota
-- warm the first query:
1
2
-- denied hit after revoking SELECT:
ACCESS_DENIED
-- the second query enters the released quota:
10
20
-- the second query now hits:
10
20
